# Quiz generator QA optimization pass

Use when the user asks for a **QA pass**, **optimization pass**, or to tune `quiz-generator.php`.

## Trigger QA runs (agent — after QA_RUN_TOKEN is in server dblogin.php)

One run per POST (~7 min) to avoid gateway timeouts; repeat 3× for a full pass:

```bash
curl.exe -sk -X POST "https://quizzical.co.nz/action-qa-generate-quiz.php" ^
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" ^
  -d "{\"token\":\"TOKEN\",\"type\":\"morning\",\"runs\":1,\"lookback\":5}"
```

Response JSON includes `summary_file` and per-run `saved_to` paths on the server under `logs/qa/`. Files are **not** web-accessible (`.htaccess` deny).

CLI alternative (cPanel): `php qa-generate-quiz.php morning --runs=3 --save=logs/qa`

## Agent loop

1. POST to trigger 3 runs (or ask user to run CLI once if token not set yet).
2. Read returned JSON (questions + log + stats in response body).
3. Patch `quiz-generator.php` for recurring patterns.
4. Commit, push, deploy (see `deploy-after-push.mdc`).
5. Re-run 3 if needed; summarize for user.

## Server setup (one time)

Add to **server** `dblogin.php` (gitignored):

```php
define('QA_RUN_TOKEN', 'your-long-random-token');
```

Use the same token in agent curl commands. Deploy does not overwrite `dblogin.php`.

## User kickoff

> Run an optimization pass.

User does not paste quiz output. They only say whether to run another pass.
